# Copy to .env and fill in with your own Supabase project's values
# (Project Settings > API Keys in the Supabase dashboard — the
# "Publishable key"; older projects may label it "anon" / "anon public"
# instead, which is the same kind of key under a name Supabase is
# retiring). Without these set, the app runs entirely on mock auth and
# sample challenge data — see README.md "The backend (Supabase)".
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# The "Web application" OAuth client ID from Google Cloud Console — see
# README.md "Google Sign-In (native)" for what else it needs (an iOS
# client, an Android client, and app.json's iosUrlScheme). Only read when
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL/PUBLISHABLE_KEY above are also set — if Supabase isn't
# configured, Google sign-in (like everything else) uses mock auth
# instead and doesn't need this at all. If Supabase IS configured but
# this isn't, tapping Google shows a clear "needs this env var" error
# rather than silently falling back.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=your-web-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# The "iOS" OAuth client ID from the same Google Cloud Console project —
# NOT the same value as the Web client ID above, and required on iOS
# specifically (the native SDK has no other way to learn its client ID
# without a Firebase GoogleService-Info.plist, which this project doesn't
# use). This is the plain client ID
# ("1234-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com"); app.json's iosUrlScheme needs
# the *reversed* form of this same value
# ("com.googleusercontent.apps.1234-abc") — same OAuth client, two
# different places it has to be spelled out. Not needed on Android.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=your-ios-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# RevenueCat's per-platform *public* SDK keys (RevenueCat dashboard:
# Project Settings > API Keys — the "Public app-specific API key" for
# each app, not the Secret key). These are safe in the app bundle the
# same way the Google client IDs above are — they only let the SDK read
# offerings and record purchases as this installed app, not touch anyone
# else's account. The Secret key and the webhook's shared secret are
# server-side only: set them as Supabase Edge Function secrets
# (`supabase secrets set REVENUECAT_SECRET_API_KEY=... REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...`),
# never here. Only read once the Bones purchase UI exists (fast-follow to
# the Bones shop, see mobile/supabase/migrations/0064_bones_purchases.sql)
# — until then the app runs fine without them, same "not configured,
# feature quietly does without" story as the Google keys above.
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=appl_...
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY=goog_...
